WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.505
Deploying a detection is an operational change.

00:00:02.505 --> 00:00:05.597
Teams should consider whether the detection will alert immediately,

00:00:05.597 --> 00:00:09.720
whether it should run silently first, and who will monitor early behavior.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:14.530
A rollout should also define which playbook applies, how analysts will interpret the signal,

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.279
and how unexpected alert volume will be handled.

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:18.653
Careful deployment reduces surprise.

00:00:18.653 --> 00:00:23.807
It gives teams a chance to understand real-world behavior before relying on the detection fully.

00:00:23.807 --> 00:00:25.525
Managed rollout also supports trust.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:30.679
Analysts are more likely to use a new detection well when they understand its purpose,

00:00:30.679 --> 00:00:32.740
severity, expected context, and escalation path.
